WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:10.909
This is Tide Wave, a personal project: a practice tool for intraday trading that I built with AI, mostly with Claude.

2
00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:17.429
It replays a past trading day minute by minute, so I can practise decisions with no money at risk.

3
00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:22.394
A practice never reaches a broker. Nothing here is financial advice.

4
00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:27.771
Rehearse lists past days whose last five sessions look most like the coming session.

5
00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:35.381
Pick a day opens the list of training days. For this demo, I use July 27, 2021.

6
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:40.878
The chart stays covered until I press Start, so I cannot peek at how the day ends.

7
00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:44.311
I choose Training mode and press Start practice.

8
00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:48.461
Now the day replays from the open, one minute at a time.

9
00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:54.167
When one of the system's strategies wants to trade, an ask appears on the card at the right.

10
00:00:55.070 --> 00:01:02.500
Each row is a reading at that minute: the entry turn, the central line, the trend walk, the two-year bond, and option flow.

11
00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:09.530
On the live card, a small bot face also gives the practice agent's opinion. It never answers for me.

12
00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:14.795
I answer YES to take the trade, or NO to skip it. Here I say yes.

13
00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:21.505
A few minutes later, the strategy asks to exit. I approve, and the practice position is sold.

14
00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:28.447
The boundary button joins the recent highs and lows into trend lines, as they form, with no hindsight.

15
00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:35.225
Drawing tools, a trend line, ray, level and channel, let me mark my own view on the chart.

16
00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:41.321
Fast forward skips ahead. Every minute is still replayed, and it stops at the next ask.

17
00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:44.774
This time I say no, and skip the entry.

18
00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:51.382
At the end, the day is scored: my calls beside the machine's, and whether each trade won or lost.

19
00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:57.435
The point is practice: to watch a day unfold, and compare my judgment with the system's.

20
00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:04.901
Thanks for watching. This is a personal learning project, not financial advice, and no trading code is shared.

